# Closet / Wishlist / Profile grid — tab path routes (not item: + clear-on-appear)

## Problem (iOS 18 / 26)

`navigationDestination(item: $…)` with `.onAppear { binding = nil }` blank-flashes and pops on newer iOS. The binding becoming `nil` means “pop.” That pattern looked fine on iOS 17 but fails on iOS 26.

## Fix (same as Calendar / Profile)

Closet and Wishlist own `NavigationStack(path: $navigationPath)`. Register **one** `navigationDestination(for: ItemGridFilterRoute.self)` that covers:

| Push | Route |
|---|---|
| Filter (items) | `.itemFilter` |
| Filter (outfits) | `.outfitFilter` |
| + → ItemAddView | `.addItem` |
| Queued multi-add → ItemAddView | `.addItemQueued` |
| Outfits + → OutfitAddView | `.addOutfit(sessionID:)` |
| Grid / pair → ItemDetailView | `.itemDetail(uri:)` |
| Grid / item outfits → OutfitDetailView | `.outfitDetail(uri:)` |
| Item detail Create Outfit | `.createOutfitFromItem(itemURI:sessionID:)` |
| Items Pack → ItemPackView | `.packing` |
| Pack Checklist → PackingChecklistView | `.packingChecklist` |
| OutfitAddView “View Existing” duplicate | `.outfitDetail(uri:)` (reuse) |

Profile owns pending Redress on `ProfileRoute.pendingRedress(...)`.

- Toolbar / grid / detail / OutfitAddView only `navigationPath.append(...)`.
- Leave path entries until system Back / `dismiss()`.
- Do **not** nil route bindings in `onAppear`.

`ItemGridView` requests pushes via `onOpenAddItem` / `onOpenAddOutfit` / `onOpenItemDetail` / `onOpenOutfitDetail` / `onOpenPacking` / `onOpenPendingRedress` (and filter callbacks). When those callbacks are set, it does **not** register the matching `navigationDestination(item:)`.

`ItemDetailView` / `OutfitDetailView` / `OutfitAddView` take optional `navigationPath`. When set (Closet/Wishlist), nested Create Outfit / pair / outfit / duplicate-existing taps append routes. When nil (Profile, Redress, sheets, etc.), keep local `item:` destinations.

Item Detail **Edit Image** is currently a **sheet** (nested `item:` froze). Path-route crop/edit for Item Detail + Item Add is **deferred** — see `item-edit-image-path-route-deferred.mdc`. Do not convert Outfit or non-tab-path hosts.

Queued add shares `ImageQueueCoordinator` owned by Closet/Wishlist so crop → Add Item → next crop still works after path pop.

## Don’t

- `NavigationLink(destination: ItemAddView…)` on the Closet toolbar
- `navigationDestination(item: $itemAddNavigation)` / `$outfitAddNavigation` / `$packingNavigation` / detail bindings + clear-on-appear on the Closet/Wishlist stack
- Nesting another `NavigationStack` inside Add Item / Add Outfit for these tab pushes
